   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The relation gives \\( f'(0) = 0 \\). Differentiate the relation, using the product rule and the chain rule on each term that holds \\( f \\): \\( f'' = f^{2} + 2 f f' x \\), then \\( f''' = 4 f f' + 2 f f'' x + 2 f'^{2} x \\).",
         "mathjson": 0
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Evaluate in order at \\( x = 0 \\), feeding each value into the next: \\( f'(0) = 0 \\), \\( f''(0) = 4 \\), \\( f'''(0) = 0 \\).",
         "mathjson": 0
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Divide each value by the matching factorial: \\( \\frac{2}{0!} = 2 \\), \\( \\frac{0}{1!} = 0 \\), \\( \\frac{4}{2!} = 2 \\), \\( \\frac{0}{3!} = 0 \\).",
